# Exception: this one is POLICY, not runtime state. It is the authorization
# registry for scripts/protocols/agent-self-edit-gate.cjs, and the gate cannot
# run without it — which is exactly why that gate sat at zero call sites. The
# chronological control plane vanished the same way (gitignored, unrecoverable
# from git, every cron job exiting 0 for ~11 weeks). Policy that gates authority
# must be reviewable in history. See
# docs/protocols/reports/silent-failure-audit-2026-08-05.md.
!data/protocols/agent-owned-docs.registry.json
# Exception: the SYSTEM half of the process schedule. scope=system_framework
# only — the platform's own cron, SUPER_ADMIN-owned, containing no operator
# data (verified: no emails, home paths, credentials or names). It ships with
# TNF and must be recoverable by any clone; when the merged registry was
# gitignored and vanished, every job threw "not registered" and exited 0 for
# ~11 weeks with nothing to restore from.
#
# The TENANT half deliberately lives OUTSIDE this repo, at
# ~/.config/tnf/processes.json, so an operator's private automation is never
# published. cron-jobs.registry.json and chronological-process-catalog.json
# remain ignored: they are GENERATED from both stores by
# scripts/protocols/build-process-registry.cjs and are reconstructible, not
# authoritative.
!data/protocols/system-processes.json
