# ── Process atlas: generated runtime snapshots ───────────────────────────────
# These are regenerated locally by .verifier/generate-process-atlas.py and
# capture live `pgrep -fl` command lines. The generator redacts credentials,
# but a process snapshot of the operator's machine is runtime state, not
# source — it does not belong in the tree. (.verifier is already in
# ALWAYS_EXCLUDE in scripts/sync-repos.sh; this closes the private-repo side.)
.verifier/process-atlas.payload.json
.verifier/process-atlas.digest.md
.verifier/process-atlas.verify.json
.verifier/tnf-process-atlas.html

# Cross-agent parity ledger — regenerated by `tnf parity audit` and by every
# `tnf self-improvement run` cycle. Output, not source: tracking it would dirty
# the working tree on every hourly full-auto cycle.
docs/operations/parity/

# Generated extension icons. Both extensions build these in `prebuild` via
# generate-icons.cjs + scripts/generate-notification-icons.cjs, and their
# `clean` scripts delete them by design. They were committed anyway, so the
# hourly `pnpm run clean` cron destroyed 36 tracked files every hour and git
# reported them as deletions — noise that twice made a genuine asset question
# indistinguishable from routine churn. Verified 2026-08-05: deleting icons/
# and running both generators reproduces every file byte-identical to HEAD.
apps/chrome-extension/icons/
apps/gemini-bridge-extension/icons/

# M&A paperwork — sensitive business material with operator's real name.
